["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"ess","stream_identity":"01a0d3e0-4003-757b-b72c-9441fdf06fca","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"specification","fields":{"body":"# Specification: Static-server-safe generated documentation paths\n\n## Context\n\nThis record migrates `beyond10x/ess` GitHub issue 2, “ess generate --kind docs emits filenames a static server cannot serve.” The issue was opened by `the operator` on 2026-09-02 at 14:12:51Z, remained open with no labels, assignees, milestone, or comments, and described dotted domain names becoming dotted path segments that static servers interpret as extension-bearing filenames.\n\nNo implementation was added during this migration. Current `main` already satisfies the issue through commit `6cd3706ee2530a1806e74f169851d23667b2bdb7`, released in ESS 0.4.0 and every later release through 0.9.2. The implementation explains and performs the transformation at `crates/ess-gen/src/docs.rs:2502-2511`; generated-document tests exercise hyphenated domain paths beginning at `crates/ess-gen/tests/docs.rs:308`.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. A domain page generated by `ess generate --kind docs` uses a static-server-safe path stem.\n2. Every dot in the qualified domain name becomes a hyphen in the path stem, so `acd.routing` is emitted as `domains/acd-routing.md`.\n3. Links generated for that domain use the same transformed page identity.\n4. The page content and title retain the qualified domain name; only its route identity changes.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The transformation is deterministic and does not depend on a particular static-site generator.\n- The generated Markdown extension remains `.md`; only dots within the route stem are transformed.\n- A consumer must not need a post-processing rename-and-rewrite pass.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Choosing a documentation site theme or static-site framework.\n- Renaming the domain inside the ESS model.\n- The broader `--kind site` projection that landed in the same implementation commit.\n\n## Invariants\n\n- A qualified domain name maps to one stable page identity everywhere the generator writes or links it.\n- A route stem generated from a dotted domain contains no dot.\n- Repeated generation from the same ESS IR produces the same paths and links.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Generating documentation for `acd.routing` produces `domains/acd-routing.md`, never `domains/acd.routing.md`.\n- Every link targeting the generated page resolves to the hyphenated path.\n- `task check` passes at the migrated repository revision.\n\n## Resolution\n\nImplemented before migration by `6cd3706ee2530a1806e74f169851d23667b2bdb7` and included in the published 0.4.0 release. This migration records the already-delivered behavior; it does not build it again.\n\n## Ambiguities\n\n- `inferable` — the requested filename mapping is explicit in the issue and in `domain_page_id` at `crates/ess-gen/src/docs.rs:2509-2510`.\n- `inferable` — the behavior is released: `git tag --contains 6cd3706` includes 0.4.0 through 0.9.2.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone.\n\n## Original GitHub Issue\n\nSource: `https://github.com/beyond10x/ess/issues/2`\n\n> `ess generate --kind docs` writes one page per domain, named after the domain. A domain called\n> `acd.routing` becomes `domains/acd.routing.md`, and the site built from it serves\n> `domains/acd.routing/`.\n>\n> A static file server reads the dot as an extension boundary and returns 404 for that path. This is\n> not a Docusaurus quirk — GitLab Pages, GitHub Pages and `http-server` all behave this way, because\n> the segment looks like a filename.\n>\n> **Observed** on `an adopting project`, whose ESS model declares `acd.routing` and `acd.backend`. The published\n> site 404s on both domain pages until the stems are renamed and every link to them rewritten. The\n> repository carries that rename as a post-processing pass in `scripts/build-docs.sh`, which is a\n> workaround every consumer of `--kind docs` with a dotted domain name will have to write.\n>\n> ### What would fix it\n>\n> Emit the dot as something a path segment can carry — `domains/acd-routing.md` — and write the links\n> to match. The page's title still says `acd.routing`; only the filename changes.\n\n## Provenance\n\nMigrated from GitHub issue `beyond10x/ess#2`.\n\n- Created 2026-09-02T14:12:51Z · last updated 2026-09-02T14:12:51Z\n- Original state: `OPEN`\n- Original author: `the operator`\n- Original issue body: 21 lines, 15 nonblank\n- Original labels, assignees, milestone, comments, and issue relations: none\n- AEP reference: `github:beyond10x/ess#2`\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-da316bbb2849d4ec89cfc1fc6f6823ff","locator":"ep://planning/store/specification/static-server-safe-generated-doc-paths","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.specification/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Specification: Static-server-safe generated documentation paths\n\n## Context\n\nThis record migrates `beyond10x/ess` GitHub issue 2, “ess generate --kind docs emits filenames a static server cannot serve.” The issue was opened by `the operator` on 2026-09-02 at 14:12:51Z, remained open with no labels, assignees, milestone, or comments, and described dotted domain names becoming dotted path segments that static servers interpret as extension-bearing filenames.\n\nNo implementation was added during this migration. Current `main` already satisfies the issue through commit `6cd3706ee2530a1806e74f169851d23667b2bdb7`, released in ESS 0.4.0 and every later release through 0.9.2. The implementation explains and performs the transformation at `crates/ess-gen/src/docs.rs:2502-2511`; generated-document tests exercise hyphenated domain paths beginning at `crates/ess-gen/tests/docs.rs:308`.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. A domain page generated by `ess generate --kind docs` uses a static-server-safe path stem.\n2. Every dot in the qualified domain name becomes a hyphen in the path stem, so `acd.routing` is emitted as `domains/acd-routing.md`.\n3. Links generated for that domain use the same transformed page identity.\n4. The page content and title retain the qualified domain name; only its route identity changes.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The transformation is deterministic and does not depend on a particular static-site generator.\n- The generated Markdown extension remains `.md`; only dots within the route stem are transformed.\n- A consumer must not need a post-processing rename-and-rewrite pass.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Choosing a documentation site theme or static-site framework.\n- Renaming the domain inside the ESS model.\n- The broader `--kind site` projection that landed in the same implementation commit.\n\n## Invariants\n\n- A qualified domain name maps to one stable page identity everywhere the generator writes or links it.\n- A route stem generated from a dotted domain contains no dot.\n- Repeated generation from the same ESS IR produces the same paths and links.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Generating documentation for `acd.routing` produces `domains/acd-routing.md`, never `domains/acd.routing.md`.\n- Every link targeting the generated page resolves to the hyphenated path.\n- `task check` passes at the migrated repository revision.\n\n## Resolution\n\nImplemented before migration by `6cd3706ee2530a1806e74f169851d23667b2bdb7` and included in the published 0.4.0 release. This migration records the already-delivered behavior; it does not build it again.\n\n## Ambiguities\n\n- `inferable` — the requested filename mapping is explicit in the issue and in `domain_page_id` at `crates/ess-gen/src/docs.rs:2509-2510`.\n- `inferable` — the behavior is released: `git tag --contains 6cd3706` includes 0.4.0 through 0.9.2.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone.\n\n## Original GitHub Issue\n\nSource: `https://github.com/beyond10x/ess/issues/2`\n\n> `ess generate --kind docs` writes one page per domain, named after the domain. A domain called\n> `acd.routing` becomes `domains/acd.routing.md`, and the site built from it serves\n> `domains/acd.routing/`.\n>\n> A static file server reads the dot as an extension boundary and returns 404 for that path. This is\n> not a Docusaurus quirk — GitLab Pages, GitHub Pages and `http-server` all behave this way, because\n> the segment looks like a filename.\n>\n> **Observed** on `an adopting project`, whose ESS model declares `acd.routing` and `acd.backend`. The published\n> site 404s on both domain pages until the stems are renamed and every link to them rewritten. The\n> repository carries that rename as a post-processing pass in `scripts/build-docs.sh`, which is a\n> workaround every consumer of `--kind docs` with a dotted domain name will have to write.\n>\n> ### What would fix it\n>\n> Emit the dot as something a path segment can carry — `domains/acd-routing.md` — and write the links\n> to match. The page's title still says `acd.routing`; only the filename changes.\n\n## Provenance\n\nMigrated from GitHub issue `beyond10x/ess#2`.\n\n- Created 2026-09-02T14:12:51Z · last updated 2026-09-02T14:12:51Z\n- Original state: `OPEN`\n- Original author: `the operator`\n- Original issue body: 21 lines, 15 nonblank\n- Original labels, assignees, milestone, comments, and issue relations: none\n- AEP reference: `github:beyond10x/ess#2`\n","owner":"ess","refs":[{"provider":"github","reference":"beyond10x/ess#2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Generated domain documentation uses a stable path that static file servers can serve.","tags":["github-issue-migration"],"title":"Static-server-safe generated documentation paths"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"owner":"ess","refs":[{"provider":"github","reference":"beyond10x/ess#2"}],"summary":"Generated domain documentation uses a stable path that static file servers can serve.","tags":["github-issue-migration"],"title":"Static-server-safe generated d